---
name: brand-positioning-kit
description: Use when defining or refining brand concept, tone, positioning, audience desire, taboo/tension, messaging pillars, or wiki-ready brand guidelines for any venture. Especially useful before creating landing pages, instructor profiles, course offers, social series, or OpenClaw creative briefs.
---

# Brand Positioning Kit

Use this skill before producing major marketing assets. The output should make future content easier to generate, not just describe the brand.

## Read First

When a venture or product is named, read available wiki/repo context before inventing brand rules. Look for:

- existing brand or product docs.
- founder notes and business strategy.
- landing pages, app copy, README, CLAUDE.md, design docs.
- previous user feedback in `~/.sj-agent-harness/evals/feedback.jsonl` if available.

## Positioning Components

Define:

- audience and anti-audience.
- urgent pain and hidden desire.
- promise and proof.
- enemy or tension.
- voice: sentence rhythm, word choice, taboo level, emotional temperature.
- repeatable slogans, frames, and content territories.
- what to avoid because it sounds generic, fake, or off-brand.

## Venture Defaults

- ZERO-ONE: AI/vibe-coding education that makes beginners build real products and makes advanced users systematize output.
- D-EDU: learning, math thinking, student/parent trust, practical academic improvement.
- ROMEO/CUPID/DARK: dating, attraction, relationship psychology, clean versus dark positioning.
- 해낼게: public commitment, support, identity shift, friends pushing friends forward.
- 단타해줘/JOGON 경제: news-to-understanding, economic literacy, AI experiment, not investment advice.

## Output

```markdown
## Brand Positioning Kit

### 1. Core Position
- one-liner:
- audience:
- anti-audience:
- promise:
- proof:
- enemy/tension:

### 2. Tone System
- voice:
- emotional temperature:
- words to use:
- words to avoid:
- provocative edge:

### 3. Messaging Pillars
| pillar | message | proof | content examples |
|---|---|---|---|

### 4. Asset Guidance
- landing page:
- instructor profile:
- social posts:
- OpenClaw brief:

### 5. Wiki Update Suggestion
- page:
- section:
- bullets:
```

## Rubric (의무 — 2026-07-12 품질헌법 연동)

- 산출 전 `/Users/sj/.claude/standards/branding.md` + `/Users/sj/.claude/standards/writing.md` Read 필수. 산출물 끝 `RUBRIC_SCORE` + `WEAKEST_LINE` 푸터 의무.
- **경쟁사 치환 테스트 (핵심 게이트)**: 포지셔닝 문장·슬로건에 경쟁사 이름을 넣어도 성립하면 폐기·재작성. 브랜드 정의 최소 세트(포지셔닝 1문장·톤 3형용사+반례·금기 3+·긴장 1+·개봉 장면 1컷) 전부 채울 것 — branding.md §3.

## Worked Examples — GOOD/BAD (한국어, 자사 실작)

- 포지셔닝 BAD "최고의 IT 교육을 제공합니다" (누구나 가능 = FAIL) → GOOD **"성공담은 없습니다. 순서는 있습니다"** (ZERO-ONE — 실패 고백 자산 없인 못 쓰는 문장)
- 슬로건 BAD "함께 성장하는 응원 플랫폼" → GOOD **"응원은 돈으로 하는 겁니다"** (해낼게 — 철학이 긴장을 감수)
- 톤 형용사+반례 GOOD: **"따뜻한 — 단 유치하지 않게(반말 남발 금지)"** 식으로 형용사마다 "이건 아님"을 짝 지을 것 (zero-one DESIGN.md 3앵커 방식)
- 청중 분기 GOOD: 같은 사실을 100B(건조 포스트모템)/ZERO-ONE(직접화법 "당신")/IR(회계 어휘 "검증 비용")로 갈라 쓴 100b 브랜드스토리 — 일관성 = 같은 톤 복붙이 아니라 같은 정체성의 채널별 개봉.

